-- Q++ 0.2
module exchange
uses theory, clusters

subsection sec:exchange The unit tie of two exponents

-- An orbit of positive masses \(x_1,y_1,x_2,y_2,\dots\) tied by the unit, \(x_ix_{i+1}=y_i^c+1\) and
-- \(y_iy_{i+1}=x_{i+1}^b+1\). With the exponent \(0\) at every other place the ties read \(x_0x_2=2\) and
-- \(x_1x_3=x_2^c+1\): four steps fix \(x_0\) and carry \(x_1\) to \(x_5\) with \(x_5(x_2^c+1)=x_1(x_0^c+1)\) (mixed).
-- The two agree only where \(x_2=x_0\), that is \(x_0^2=2\), so over \(\mathbb Q_{>0}\) the orbit does not return in
-- four steps (mixedq), while the point \(x_0^2=2\) of the line returns. Powers of two masses keep their order (core
-- power), so \(x_2^c=x_0^c\) only where \(x_2=x_0\). An orbit that returns after \(P\) pairs ties the products of one
-- period, \(X=\prod x_i\) and \(Y=\prod y_i\): \(X^2=\prod(y_i^c+1)>Y^c\) and \(Y^2=\prod(x_{i+1}^b+1)>X^b\), the
-- unit making each strict, so \(Y^4>X^{2b}>Y^{bc}\) with \(Y\ge1\), and the exponents satisfy \(bc\le3\) (period).
lemma lem:exchange [the unit tie of two exponents]
  core power: c in NN>=1, a, b in QQ>0, a < b : a^c < b^c
  fix core power exchange.power
  neqfix core power exchange.power.nolt
  (mixed): c in NN>=1, x0, x1, x2, x3, x4, x5 in QQ>0, x0 * x2 = 2, x1 * x3 = x2^c + 1, x2 * x4 = 2, x3 * x5 = x4^c + 1 : x4 = x0, x5 * (x2^c + 1) = x1 * (x0^c + 1)
  fix (mixed) exchange.mixed
  neqfix (mixed) exchange.mixed.nothird
  (mixedq): c in NN>=1, x0, x1, x2, x3, x4, x5 in QQ>0, x0 * x2 = 2, x1 * x3 = x2^c + 1, x2 * x4 = 2, x3 * x5 = x4^c + 1 : x5 != x1
  fix (mixedq) exchange.mixedq
  neqfix (mixedq) exchange.mixedq.nothird
  (period): P, b, c in NN>=1, x_(1..P + 1), y_(1..P + 1) in QQ>0, (forall i in NN>=1 : i <= P => x_(i) * x_(i + 1) = y_(i)^c + 1), (forall i in NN>=1 : i <= P => y_(i) * y_(i + 1) = x_(i + 1)^b + 1), x_(P + 1) = x_(1), y_(P + 1) = y_(1) : b * c <= 3
  fix (period) exchange.period
  neqfix (period) exchange.period.noreturn
  origin: ?{\text{proved here with no claim of novelty: the exchange relation of rank two with one exponent zero, and the bound \(bc\le3\) for a positive orbit that returns; for \(bc\le3\) these are the recurrences of the cluster algebras of rank two of finite type (Fomin and Zelevinsky)}}

-- One more factor keeps the order of the powers (core power). The third tie gives \(x_4=x_0\), and then the fourth
-- over the second is the ratio of the step (mixed). A return \(x_5=x_1\) ties \(x_2^c\) to \(x_0^c\), so neither
-- \(x_2<x_0\) nor \(x_0<x_2\), and \(x_2=x_0\) makes \(x_0^2=2\), which no rational satisfies (mixedq). Over one period
-- the shifted products equal the products, by the return; the ties multiply to \(X^2=\prod(y_i^c+1)\) and
-- \(Y^2=\prod(x_{i+1}^b+1)\), each above the product of the powers by its first factor; so \(Y^2\ge1\), \(Y\ge1\), and
-- the powers keep their order (core power) up to \(Y^{bc}<Y^4\), which \(4\le bc\) and \(Y\ge1\) forbid (period).
proof lem:exchange
  "core power" ind[c; V[1 * h_1]; with[a^c * a < b^c * b by mono; V[1 * hw1]]]
  (mixed) with[x2 * x4 = x2 * x0 by V[1 * h_3 | 1 * h_1]; with[x4 = x0 by div[x2]; with[x4^c = x0^c by eq; (V[1 * hw2], V[x5 * h_2, x1 * h_4, x1 * hw3])]]]
  (mixedq) with[x5 * (x2^c + 1) = x1 * (x0^c + 1) by with[(x4 = x0, x5 * (x2^c + 1) = x1 * (x0^c + 1)) by lem:exchange(mixed)[c := c, x0 := x0, x1 := x1, x2 := x2, x3 := x3, x4 := x4, x5 := x5]; logic]; cases[x5 = x1; with[x1 * x2^c = x1 * x0^c by V[1 * hw1 | (x2^c + 1) * hc1]; with[x2^c = x0^c by div[x1]; cases[x2 < x0; with[x2^c < x0^c by lem:exchange(core power)[c := c, a := x2, b := x0]; with[x0^c <= x2^c by V[| 1 * hw4]; logic]]; cases[x0 < x2; with[x0^c < x2^c by lem:exchange(core power)[c := c, a := x0, b := x2]; with[x2^c <= x0^c by V[1 * hw4]; logic]]; with[x2 = x0 by V[1 * hn3], V[1 * hn2]; with[x0^2 != 2 by fact:sqrttwo(1)[c := x0]; with[x0^2 = 2 by V[x0 * hw9, 1 * h_1]; logic]]]]]]]; logic]]
  (period) with[1 <= P + 1 by V; with[(prod i in 1..P + 1, x_(i)) = (prod i in 1..P, x_(i)) * x_(P + 1) by sum; with[(prod i in 1..P + 1, x_(i)) = x_(1) * (prod i in 1 + 1..P + 1, x_(i)) by sum; with[(prod i in 1..P, x_(i + 1)) = (prod i in 1 + 1..P + 1, x_(i)) by sum; with[x_(1) * (prod i in 1..P, x_(i + 1)) = x_(1) * (prod i in 1..P, x_(i)) by V[x_(1) * hw4, 1 * hw2, (prod i in 1..P, x_(i)) * h_3 | 1 * hw3]; with[(prod i in 1..P, x_(i + 1)) = (prod i in 1..P, x_(i)) by div[x_(1)]; with[(prod i in 1..P + 1, y_(i)) = (prod i in 1..P, y_(i)) * y_(P + 1) by sum; with[(prod i in 1..P + 1, y_(i)) = y_(1) * (prod i in 1 + 1..P + 1, y_(i)) by sum; with[(prod i in 1..P, y_(i + 1)) = (prod i in 1 + 1..P + 1, y_(i)) by sum; with[y_(1) * (prod i in 1..P, y_(i + 1)) = y_(1) * (prod i in 1..P, y_(i)) by V[y_(1) * hw9, 1 * hw7, (prod i in 1..P, y_(i)) * h_4 | 1 * hw8]; with[(prod i in 1..P, y_(i + 1)) = (prod i in 1..P, y_(i)) by div[y_(1)]; with[(prod i in 1..P, x_(i) * x_(i + 1)) = (prod i in 1..P, (y_(i)^c + 1)) by sum[V]; with[(prod i in 1..P, x_(i) * x_(i + 1)) = (prod i in 1..P, x_(i)) * (prod i in 1..P, x_(i + 1)) by sum; with[(prod i in 1..P, (y_(i)^c + 1)) = (y_(1)^c + 1) * (prod i in 1 + 1..P, (y_(i)^c + 1)) by sum; with[(prod i in 1..P, y_(i)^c) = y_(1)^c * (prod i in 1 + 1..P, y_(i)^c) by sum; with[(prod i in 1 + 1..P, y_(i)^c) <= (prod i in 1 + 1..P, (y_(i)^c + 1)) by mono; with[y_(1)^c < y_(1)^c + 1 by V; with[y_(1)^c * (prod i in 1 + 1..P, y_(i)^c) < (y_(1)^c + 1) * (prod i in 1 + 1..P, (y_(i)^c + 1)) by mono; with[(prod i in 1..P, y_(i)^c) = (prod i in 1..P, y_(i))^c by eq; with[(prod i in 1..P, y_(i))^c < (prod i in 1..P, x_(i)) * (prod i in 1..P, x_(i)) by V[1 * hw18, 1 * hw15, 1 * hw13, (prod i in 1..P, x_(i)) * hw6 | 1 * hw14, 1 * hw19, 1 * hw12]; with[(prod i in 1..P, y_(i) * y_(i + 1)) = (prod i in 1..P, (x_(i + 1)^b + 1)) by sum[V]; with[(prod i in 1..P, y_(i) * y_(i + 1)) = (prod i in 1..P, y_(i)) * (prod i in 1..P, y_(i + 1)) by sum; with[(prod i in 1..P, (x_(i + 1)^b + 1)) = (x_(1 + 1)^b + 1) * (prod i in 1 + 1..P, (x_(i + 1)^b + 1)) by sum; with[(prod i in 1..P, x_(i + 1)^b) = x_(1 + 1)^b * (prod i in 1 + 1..P, x_(i + 1)^b) by sum; with[(prod i in 1 + 1..P, x_(i + 1)^b) <= (prod i in 1 + 1..P, (x_(i + 1)^b + 1)) by mono; with[x_(1 + 1)^b < x_(1 + 1)^b + 1 by V; with[x_(1 + 1)^b * (prod i in 1 + 1..P, x_(i + 1)^b) < (x_(1 + 1)^b + 1) * (prod i in 1 + 1..P, (x_(i + 1)^b + 1)) by mono; with[(prod i in 1..P, x_(i + 1)^b) = (prod i in 1..P, x_(i + 1))^b by eq; with[(prod i in 1..P, x_(i))^b <= (prod i in 1..P, x_(i + 1))^b by mono; with[(prod i in 1..P, x_(i))^b < (prod i in 1..P, y_(i)) * (prod i in 1..P, y_(i)) by V[1 * hw27, 1 * hw24, 1 * hw22, (prod i in 1..P, y_(i)) * hw11, 1 * hw29 | 1 * hw23, 1 * hw28, 1 * hw21]; with[1 <= (prod i in 1..P, (x_(i + 1)^b + 1)) by mono; with[(1 + (prod i in 1..P, y_(i))) * 1 <= (1 + (prod i in 1..P, y_(i))) * (prod i in 1..P, y_(i)) by V[(prod i in 1..P, y_(i)) * hw11, 1 * hw22, 1 * hw31 | 1 * hw21]; with[1 <= (prod i in 1..P, y_(i)) by div[1 + (prod i in 1..P, y_(i))]; with[0 < (prod i in 1..P, x_(i))^b by mono; with[0 < (prod i in 1..P, y_(i)) * (prod i in 1..P, y_(i)) by mono; with[0 < (prod i in 1..P, y_(i))^c by mono; with[0 < (prod i in 1..P, x_(i)) * (prod i in 1..P, x_(i)) by mono; with[((prod i in 1..P, x_(i))^b)^2 < ((prod i in 1..P, y_(i)) * (prod i in 1..P, y_(i)))^2 by lem:exchange(core power)[c := 2, a := (prod i in 1..P, x_(i))^b, b := (prod i in 1..P, y_(i)) * (prod i in 1..P, y_(i))]; with[((prod i in 1..P, y_(i))^c)^b < ((prod i in 1..P, x_(i)) * (prod i in 1..P, x_(i)))^b by lem:exchange(core power)[c := b, a := (prod i in 1..P, y_(i))^c, b := (prod i in 1..P, x_(i)) * (prod i in 1..P, x_(i))]; with[((prod i in 1..P, x_(i))^b)^2 = ((prod i in 1..P, x_(i)) * (prod i in 1..P, x_(i)))^b by V; with[((prod i in 1..P, y_(i))^c)^b = (prod i in 1..P, y_(i))^(b * c) by V; with[((prod i in 1..P, y_(i)) * (prod i in 1..P, y_(i)))^2 = (prod i in 1..P, y_(i))^4 by V; with[(prod i in 1..P, y_(i))^(b * c) < (prod i in 1..P, y_(i))^4 by V[1 * hw38, 1 * hw39, 1 * hw42 | 1 * hw40, 1 * hw41]; cases[b * c <= 3; V[1 * hc1]; with[4 <= b * c by V[1 * hn1]; with[(prod i in 1..P, y_(i))^4 <= (prod i in 1..P, y_(i))^(b * c) by mono; logic]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]
